---
import Detail from '../layouts/Detail.astro';
import DetailSection from '../components/DetailSection.astro';
import BankTiles from '../components/BankTiles.astro';
import AlertArt from '../components/detail/AlertArt.astro';
import Review from '../components/detail/Review.astro';
import { MAIL_NOTE } from '../data/site';
---

<Detail
  title="How it works"
  heading="How Hasala works"
  lead="Hasala reads your bank’s alert emails on your iPhone, turns each one into a transaction and sorts most of them into categories. You confirm the rest."
  path="/how-it-works"
>
  <DetailSection id="email" title="Connecting your email">
    <p>
      You give Hasala read‑only access to the email account that gets your bank’s alerts. Your iPhone asks it only for messages from your bank’s alert
      senders and reads them on the phone, so the rest of your inbox is never downloaded.
    </p>
    <p>
      Hasala can’t send, change or delete mail. Before it uses an email, your iPhone checks that it really came from your bank, and sets aside any that only looks like it did.
      No email is ever sent to an AI service.
    </p>
    <p>{MAIL_NOTE}</p>
    <AlertArt kind="mail" slot="art" />
  </DetailSection>

  <DetailSection id="banks" title="Before you start" tint>
    <p>Turn on email alerts in your banking app. Hasala reads card and account alerts from these banks:</p>
    <BankTiles detail />
    <p>Use a different bank? <a href="/#invite">Tell us which when you request an invite.</a> It helps us pick the next bank to add.</p>
  </DetailSection>

  <DetailSection id="sorting" title="How sorting works">
    <p>Each alert becomes a transaction. Hasala sorts it into a category on your iPhone, in this order:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>your own rules;</li>
      <li>a built‑in list of UAE merchants;</li>
      <li>if you turn on Cloud suggestions, a suggestion for the merchant’s name from Cloudflare’s AI service, or from Apple’s on‑device model.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>You confirm the rest. Correct a merchant once, and Hasala remembers it.</p>
    <AlertArt kind="sorted" slot="art" />
  </DetailSection>

  <Review />

  <DetailSection id="sign-in" title="Signing in" tint>
    <p>Sign in with Face ID, using a passkey, or with your email and a password.</p>
    <p>
      A password signs you in but doesn’t unlock your data on a new iPhone. Your passkey or your 12‑word recovery phrase does. See
      <a href="/how-privacy-works#new-phone">a new or lost phone</a>.
    </p>
  </DetailSection>

  <DetailSection id="iphone" title="iPhone and English only, for now">
    <p>
      Hasala does its work on the iPhone itself. Starting with one platform
      and one language lets us get every bank alert right before we promise more.
    </p>
    <p>You need an iPhone with iOS 26 or later. The app is in English and in light mode only for now.</p>
  </DetailSection>
</Detail>
